WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.060
For the first time in Legendary Entertainment's
MonsterVerse, the King of Monsters himself

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.480
shares the screen with the Eighth Wonder of
the World in Godzilla vs. Kong.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.770
The fourth epic film in the rebooted franchise
dropped on March 31st, landing both in theaters

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.560
and on HBO Max.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.939
As huge as both of these formidable behemoths
of cinema are, the battle between them is

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:24.539
a spectacle to behold no matter the size of
the screen.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:28.990
Godzilla vs. Kong takes its audience into
a new realm — specifically, Hollow Earth

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.839
— along with a group of new characters.

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:36.230
Alexander Skarsgard joins the cast as reclusive
scientist, Nathan Lind, and Rebecca Hall plays

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.649
Ilene Andrews, an advocate for King Kong who
will do whatever it takes to ensure his protection.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:45.590
Millie Bobby Brown returns to reprise her
role as Madison Russell, the young woman who

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:49.989
sets out to prove that Godzilla's motives
for destruction are not what they seem.

00:00:49.989 --> 00:00:54.629
This time Madison is joined by her friend
Josh Valentine, played by young Kiwi actor

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:56.239
Julian Dennison.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.679
But Godzilla vs. Kong has more than just new
cast members and a new story — there's also

00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:03.809
a nifty new artifact with its own bit of lore
to explore.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.250
This time, Kong has more than his giant fists
to use when pounding away at his enemies,

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.070
and we're here to talk about the mysterious
weapon discovered deep within the bowels of

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.060
Hollow Earth: King Kong's axe.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.409
It's not as if King Kong really needs a weapon,
given his sheer strength, size, and intimidating

00:01:19.409 --> 00:01:20.409
presence.

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:25.130
Yet the filmmakers of Godzilla vs. Kong decided
that the fans needed a new piece of lore to

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.420
speculate over, and the axe that appears in
the movie certainly provides one.

00:01:34.885 --> 00:01:39.755
Later, inside a grand hall within what appears
to be an ancient castle, Kong finds an axe-shaped

00:01:39.755 --> 00:01:40.885
hole in the ground.

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:45.224
As soon as Kong places the axe in its place,
the room begins to light up and the axe starts

00:01:45.224 --> 00:01:46.224
to glow.

00:01:46.224 --> 00:01:50.495
So just what is this enigmatic weapon, and
what special powers does it have?

00:01:50.495 --> 00:01:54.794
Although they are somewhat keeping mum about
the subject, Godzilla vs. Kong's director,

00:01:54.794 --> 00:01:59.684
Adam Wingard, and writer, Max Borenstein,
both spoke with Collider to give fans a few

00:01:59.684 --> 00:02:00.684
clues.

00:02:00.684 --> 00:02:01.684
Wingard hinted,

00:02:01.684 --> 00:02:05.124
"Yeah, it's something that we just kind of
tease at in the movie and hopefully we can

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.355
explore in later films."

00:02:07.355 --> 00:02:11.275
Borenstein elaborated a bit further, suggesting
that the axe was originally fashioned from

00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:15.645
the scales of a Godzilla-like creature, which
would perhaps explain how Godzilla was able

00:02:15.645 --> 00:02:19.784
to charge up the axe with his atomic breath
at the climax of the film.

00:02:19.784 --> 00:02:25.015
The writer also suggested that this axe, in
particular, was likely made just for Kong.

00:02:25.015 --> 00:02:26.295
Borenstein said,

00:02:26.295 --> 00:02:30.704
"Presumably there are more like it, but it
feels like the iconic scepter of the King."

00:02:30.704 --> 00:02:35.305
It certainly stands to reason that the giant,
glowing axe would be a weapon intended for

00:02:35.305 --> 00:02:37.855
Kong, rather than a happenstance discovery.

00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:42.555
In the movie's mythology, Kong hails from
an ancient and fallen kingdom contained within

00:02:42.555 --> 00:02:43.665
the Hollow Earth.

00:02:43.665 --> 00:02:47.655
The very fact that the axe was discovered
in this subterranean cavity — and that it

00:02:47.655 --> 00:02:51.935
interacts with the ancient castle — suggests
this deadly artifact might have once been

00:02:51.935 --> 00:02:54.064
part of the raiments of Kong's station.

00:02:54.064 --> 00:02:58.704
We're guessing Borenstein's use of the word
"scepter" is no coincidence.

00:02:58.704 --> 00:03:02.605
Borenstein has been one of the main creative
influences in Legendary's MonsterVerse since

00:03:02.605 --> 00:03:06.284
the beginning, so if anyone has the long game
in mind, it's him.

00:03:06.284 --> 00:03:10.844
Although there may be more axe mythology coming
in later films, it still plays a pivotal role

00:03:10.844 --> 00:03:13.564
in the resolution of Godzilla vs. Kong.

00:03:13.564 --> 00:03:17.265
The axe is an object that actually unites
the two titular monsters.

00:03:17.265 --> 00:03:21.505
It's an artifact from Kong's buried past,
fashioned from the body of Godzilla.

00:03:21.505 --> 00:03:25.844
In that way, the axe becomes a symbol of their
alliance to take down Mechagodzilla.

00:03:25.844 --> 00:03:30.534
Of course, it's also the literal means of
their salvation; in the climactic battle,

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:35.135
Godzilla "charges" up the axe with nuclear
breath, and Kong swings it for the win.

00:03:35.135 --> 00:03:39.185
So when will we get to learn more about the
weapon's origins in the deep recess of MonsterVerse

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.185
lore?

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:44.905
That depends on whether or not the studio
decides to make a sequel to Godzilla vs. Kong.

00:03:44.905 --> 00:03:45.905
Borenstein told Collider,

00:03:45.905 --> 00:03:50.064
"I think the MonsterVerse is at a crossroads
where audiences need to vote that they wanna

00:03:50.064 --> 00:03:53.325
see another one of these films before they
continue."

